A||||6||aubicon||87 gt trany question||||1||
Z||000000||aubicon||08-04-2001||09:42 PM||||I bought my second fiero today, an 87 gt with a 5-speed. well i checked the trany for a vin code but cannot find it. is there any other way to figue out what trany is in there? why i am asking this question is because the car will only go into neutral, 3rd and 4th gears. i am pretty sure that the culpret is the selector cable, because i can put the car into gear by operating the linkage by hand and when the cabe is removed from the stick shift the stick appears to be working fine. is this a good asumption or does any one have another idia. thanks for your time.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||08-05-2001||12:50 AM||||You idea sounds good for the selector cable.<BR>It should be a Getrag, look for the dipstick to confirm.||||reg||1
Z||000002||EdsB52||08-05-2001||03:46 AM||||The dipstick is located at the back of the transmission, toward the left side. It has a raised handle (?) that's threade into the tranny. It's pretty obvious what it is. If your tranny is bad, don't worry there are plenty of them floating around. Not really, if the tranny's good, you're looking at about $400 worth right there.||||reg||1
Z||000003||aubicon||08-05-2001||11:20 PM||||is there a letter combonation for the getrag. all that i can find on the parts lists are the mg2 and the mt2, the muncie and the isuzu.||||reg||1
Z||000004||StuGood||08-06-2001||01:10 AM||||5-speed Getrags have a steel end plate (the end farthest from the engine).  A magnet will stick to it.  The other transaxles are aluminum there - magnet won't stick.||||reg||1
Z||000005||aubicon||08-06-2001||10:49 PM||||well the magnet trick worked. it must be a getrag, but the parts lists that i am trying to order the selector cable from only list the isuzu and the muncie. is the getrag just another name for one of these. (getrag = muncie, getrag = isuzu)||||reg||1
Z||000006||LarryB||08-06-2001||11:23 PM||||The MG-2 is the 5-speed Muncie that was designed by Getrag.<BR>The MT-2 is the 5-speed Isuzu.<BR>The M-17 is the 4-speed Muncie.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by aubicon:<BR><B>well the magnet trick worked. it must be a getrag, but the parts lists that i am trying to order the selector cable from only list the isuzu and the muncie. is the getrag just another name for one of these. (getrag = muncie, getrag = isuzu)</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
